        {
          "id": "the_drive_cycle_scaffolding_is_a_single_physics_row_and_two_data_thresholds",
          "description": "The three facts W's correctness rests on that are not W itself: the braking thresholds are READ from operatingmode's Braking row rather than written as drivecycle.rs's -2.0 and -1.0 literals; exactly one physics-mapping row is selected, so dss_vsp is one polynomial and not a sum of several; and every average-speed bin's bracketing weights sum to 1, which is what catches a duplicated bracket speed or a bin with no bracket.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_brakeRate1Sec",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": -2.0,
              "coords": {
